## Task #20 (docs/specs/stdlib/executor.spec.md): block_on must
## preserve the future's Output type — not erase it to Int as the
## prior `var __block_on_res_N = 0` lowering shape did.
##
## This fixture exercises a future whose Output is Result[Int, Int].
## After block_on returns, destructuring the Result via match must
## see the Ok payload typed as Int, not as the inner-of-Int-pinned
## value the prior shape produced. The success criterion is purely
## typecheck-time: the match arm body `Ok(v) -> v + 1` requires
## `v: Int` to be visible, which is only possible if the loop
## expression's type is inferred from the `break v` value (the
## Poll.Ready payload) instead of pinned to Int by a synthesised
## result-var initializer.
##
## See compiler/riven_core/src/async_lowering/mod.rs::build_block_on_loop
## for the lowering shape this fixture pins.

async def make_result() -> Result[Int, Int]
  Ok(7)
end

def main
  let res = block_on(make_result())
  match res
    Ok(v)  -> puts "#{v + 1}"
    Err(e) -> puts "err #{e}"
  end
end
